~ core.info — facts about the build a program came from. Every member is a compile-time
~ constant, so a call costs nothing at runtime and reads no machine state.
~ Import with `<< core.info`.

~ The CPU architecture the program was built for: "aarch64", "x86_64".
>> platform = () -> Text => ""

~ The operating system it was built for: "linux", "macOS", "windows".
>> os = () -> Text => ""

~ Pointer width in bits: 64, 32.
>> bits = () -> Num => 0

~ Byte order: "little" or "big".
>> endianness = () -> Text => ""

~ The version of the Quilon compiler that built this program, e.g. "0.9.3".
>> quilonVersion = () -> Text => ""
